@startuml
' Editable visual reconstruction of the UCP AP2 checkout-flow diagram.
' Kept in sync with docs/specification/payment/extensions/ap2-mandates.md.
' The source PNG itself is not a PlantUML source file.
!pragma teoz true
scale 1.0
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam titleFontSize 15
skinparam titleFontColor #111111
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #171717
    ArrowThickness 1.1
    LifeLineBorderColor #555555
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    ParticipantBorderColor #333333
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    ParticipantFontColor #111111
    ParticipantFontSize 13
    ActorBorderColor #333333
    ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    ActorFontColor #111111
    GroupBorderColor #555555
    NoteBorderColor #C8C8C8
    NoteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    NoteFontColor #151515
    DividerFontColor #111111
    DividerFontSize 13
    DividerBorderThickness 0
    DividerBorderColor #FFFFFF
}
title AP2 Mandate Flow in UCP
actor "User" as User
participant "Platform (w/ Trusted UI)" as Platform
participant "Business Backend" as Business
participant "Credential Provider\n(Payment Handler)" as CredProvider
participant "Payment Service Provider" as PSP

== Phase 1: Discovery & Binding (The Handshake) ==
User -> Platform: "Buy this item"
Platform -> Business: POST /ucp/checkout-sessions\n(platform profile exposes "keys")
activate Business #EEEEEE
note right of Business #FFFFFF
  1. Fetch platform profile, compute
     capability intersection
  2. Detect "dev.ucp.common.payment.ap2_mandate"
     -> session is Security Locked
  3. Sign checkout: JCS(checkout minus "ap2")
     as detached JWS
end note
Business --> Platform: 201 Created (Checkout Object)\nBody: ap2.merchant_authorization = <header>..<signature>
deactivate Business
Platform -> Platform: verify_merchant_authorization()\n(reject if key unresolvable or signature invalid)

== Phase 2: User Consent & Mandate Generation ==
Platform -> User: Display Order Summary & Total\n(Rendered native by Platform)
User -> Platform: "Confirm Pay"
Platform -> Platform: Generate "Checkout Mandate" (SD-JWT+kb)\nembeds full checkout incl. ap2.merchant_authorization
Platform -> Platform: Generate "Payment Mandate" (SD-JWT+kb)
note right of Platform #FFFFFF
  Signed either by a trusted platform
  provider (server-side key) or by the
  user's wallet via OpenID4VP (+kb).
end note

== Phase 3: Payment Mandate Verification & Token Issuance ==
Platform -> CredProvider: POST /tokenize\ncredential: { type: "ap2_payment_mandate",\n  payment_mandate, checkout_jwt }\nbinding: { type: dev.ucp.shopping.checkout, id }
activate CredProvider #EEEEEE
note right of CredProvider #FFFFFF
  1. Verify mandate (SD-JWT sig, +kb, exp)
  2. Verify merchant signature on checkout_jwt
  3. Correlate hash(checkout_jwt) with the
     mandate's transaction identifier
  4. Confirm tokenization binding
end note
alt any verification step fails
    CredProvider --> Platform: Error (handler-defined surface)\nMUST NOT issue a token
else all checks pass
    CredProvider --> Platform: { "token": "tok_abc123xyz789" }\n(ordinary opaque token; mandate not embedded)
end
deactivate CredProvider

== Phase 4: Submission & Verification ==
Platform -> Business: POST /ucp/checkout-sessions/{id}/complete\n\nBody includes:\n1. ap2.checkout_mandate\n2. payment.instruments[*].credential.token
activate Business #EEEEEE
note right of Business #FFFFFF
  1. Verify "Checkout Mandate" (sig, +kb, exp)
  2. Extract embedded checkout
  3. Verify own ap2.merchant_authorization
  4. Verify terms match session state
  No credential from a verified payment
  mandate -> payment_mandate_required
end note
Business -> PSP: Process Payment (token)
activate PSP #EEEEEE
PSP -> PSP: Resolve token to the mandate it was\nissued against (already verified in Phase 3)
PSP --> Business: Success
deactivate PSP
Business -> Business: Create Order
Business --> Platform: 200 OK (Order Object)
deactivate Business
Platform -> User: Display "Order Confirmed"
@enduml
